layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "For Photo Agencies — Grosby Group"
seo_title: "For Photo Agencies — Grosby Group | Latin America Distribution Partner"
seo_description: "Partner with Grosby Group to distribute your content across Latin America and the US Hispanic market. Thirty years of dedicated licensing relationships with the region's top publishers."
permalink: /agencies/
lang: en
faq:
  - question: "What territories does Grosby Group cover?"
    answer: "We cover Latin America in full: Mexico, Central America, the Caribbean, Colombia, Venezuela, Ecuador, Peru, Bolivia, Chile, Argentina, Uruguay, Paraguay, and Brazil, plus the US Hispanic market. We have active licensing relationships in more than 20 countries across the region."
  - question: "How does an agency partnership work?"
    answer: "We act as your exclusive licensing sub-agent for Latin America and the US Hispanic market. We promote your content to our publisher network, negotiate licenses, collect fees, and remit royalties on an agreed schedule. Partnership terms are tailored to each agency. Contact us to discuss."
  - question: "Do you work with agencies that already have some Latin American relationships?"
    answer: "Yes. We regularly work with agencies that have existing regional contacts. We can structure our partnership to complement rather than conflict with your current arrangements. Talk to our team and we will find a structure that works."
  - question: "What content types are in highest demand in this market?"
    answer: "Celebrity and entertainment photography is consistently our highest-demand category. Sports, particularly football, Copa América, and Formula One, is a close second. Fashion, travel, and lifestyle content is in strong demand from magazines and digital platforms. Breaking news photography through wire services is also in constant demand."
  - question: "How are royalties calculated and remitted?"
    answer: "Royalties are calculated as a percentage of each license fee collected and remitted quarterly by bank transfer. Full transaction-level reporting is provided with each payment. Our standard payment terms are net-60 from end of quarter."
  - question: "How quickly can you bring a new agency to market?"
    answer: "Once a partnership agreement is signed and we receive your content feed or archive access, we typically begin active licensing within two to three weeks. We introduce your content to our full publisher network immediately and report on early uptake within 30 days."
